<title>TAIWAN: Walsin Lihwa slashes '96 profit forecast.</title>
<headline>Walsin Lihwa slashes '96 profit forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Walsin Lihwa Corp said on Monday it decided to slash its 1996 pre-tax profit forecast by 55.72 percent to T$650 million from an earlier prediction of T$1.468 billion.</p>
<p>Walsin Lihwa, one of Taiwan's leading electrical wire and cable makers, also cut its 1996 sales revenues forecast to T$14.324 billion from T$14.673 billion, a company statement said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
